.TH EXTRACT-REVAMPED 1 "2026-11-16" "extract-revamped" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
extract-revamped \- pick a token off the screen and type, open or copy it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B extract-revamped
.RI [ options ]
.B apply
.br
.B extract-revamped
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.B list
.br
.B extract-revamped
.RI [ options ]
.BR insert | navigate | open | copy | edit | run | choose
.RI [ pane ]
.br
.B extract-revamped doctor
.br
.B extract-revamped version
.br
.B extract-revamped help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B extract-revamped
reads the text of a tmux pane, finds the tokens of one kind in it, such as
URLs, paths, hashes or words, and hands them to fzf. The token you pick is
typed at the cursor, found in copy-mode, opened, or copied. The entry point
.B extract-revamped.tmux
runs
.B apply
once when tmux loads the plugin, and every binding goes to tmux in one call.
Each key opens a popup that runs one of the pick commands. Without
.IR pane ,
they read the client's active pane, the one under the popup, since tmux
expands no format in a popup's command. A setting given as a tmux option is
read when a pick runs; one given to
.B apply
on the command line or in the environment rides on the keys it binds.
.PP
Run with no command on a terminal, it offers a menu.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B apply
Bind the keys now.
.TP
.B list
Print every binding apply would make, one per line.
.TP
.BI insert " [pane]"
Pick a token and type it into
.I pane
with
.BR "send-keys -l" ,
so it arrives as literal text. Several marked tokens are typed joined by
spaces.
.TP
.BI navigate " [pane]"
Pick a token, put
.I pane
in copy-mode and search backward for it.
.TP
.BI open " [pane]"
Pick a token and open it: a URL through xdg-open or open, a path in
.B $EDITOR
in a new window at the pane's folder, anything else typed.
.TP
.BI copy " [pane]"
Pick a token and copy it with pbcopy, wl-copy, xclip or xsel, or as an OSC 52
sequence.
.TP
.BI edit " [pane]"
Pick a token and open it in
.B $EDITOR
in a new window at the pane's folder, whatever kind of token it is.
.TP
.BI run " [pane]"
Pick a token and start the command in
.B @extract_revamped_command
in a new window at the pane's folder, with each pick as its own argument.
Without a command it says so and exits 1.
.TP
.BI choose " [pane]"
Pick in a chooser: Enter types, C-o opens, C-y copies, C-e edits, C-x runs
your command, and C-n moves to the next mode in
.BR @extract_revamped_modes .
.TP
.B doctor
Print one row per dependency: tmux, fzf, the opener, the clipboard, base64,
gum, a default key someone else holds, and the core tools.
A settings row names any setting whose value it does not know.
Exits 1 only when a
required tool is missing.
.TP
.B version
Print the version, then the tmux version.
.TP
.B help
Print the help page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
.B list
prints one JSON object.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Colours of the terminal interface:
.BR kodougu ,
.BR catppuccin\-mocha ,
.BR catppuccin\-latte ,
.BR dracula ,
.BR nord ,
.BR gruvbox ,
.B tokyo\-night
or
.BR mono .
The default is
.BR kodougu .
.TP
.BI \-\- setting " value"
Any tmux option below, named with dashes, such as
.B \-\-mode
or
.BR \-\-min\-length .
It also takes the form
.IR \-\-setting = value .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EXTRACT_REVAMPED_SETTING
Any tmux option below in capitals, such as
.BR EXTRACT_REVAMPED_MODE .
The command line wins over the environment, and the environment over the
tmux option.
.TP
.B EXTRACT_REVAMPED_THEME
The theme when
.B \-\-theme
is not given.
.TP
.B EXTRACT_REVAMPED_ACCENT
A colour such as #CBA6F7 that replaces the accent of the theme.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_THEME
The theme of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when neither
.B \-\-theme
nor
.B EXTRACT_REVAMPED_THEME
is set.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_ACCENT
The accent of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when
.B EXTRACT_REVAMPED_ACCENT
is not set.
.TP
.B EDITOR
The editor
.B open
starts for a path,
.B vi
when unset.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns colour off in every theme.
.SH TMUX OPTIONS
An empty tmux option means its default.
.TP
.B @extract_revamped_key
The prefix key of the insert picker, or
.B none
for no key. The default is
.BR M-x ;
a key someone else already bound is left alone and
.B doctor
reports it.
.TP
.BR @extract_revamped_navigate_key ", " @extract_revamped_open_key ", " @extract_revamped_copy_key ", " @extract_revamped_edit_key ", " @extract_revamped_run_key ", " @extract_revamped_chooser_key ", " @extract_revamped_doctor_key
The prefix keys of the navigate, open, copy, edit and run pickers, the chooser
and the doctor report. All unbound by default.
.TP
.B @extract_revamped_picker
.B fzf
lists the tokens in a popup.
.B hints
covers the pane with a borderless popup, draws a letter over the start of each
token on the visible screen and acts on the one whose letter is typed, two
letters past 26 tokens; any other key closes it. It needs tmux 3.3, takes
effect after
.BR apply ,
and leaves the chooser on fzf. The default is
.BR fzf .
.TP
.B @extract_revamped_mode
What to pick:
.BR all ,
.BR urls ,
.BR paths ,
.BR words ,
.BR lines ,
.BR shas ,
.BR ipv4 ,
.BR ipv6 ,
.BR hex ,
.BR uuids ,
.BR numbers ,
.BR quoted ,
.BR bracketed ,
.BR docker ,
.BR kubernetes ,
.BR git\-status ,
.BR diff ,
.BR markdown ,
.B branches
or
.BR custom .
The default is
.BR all .
.TP
.B @extract_revamped_modes
The modes C-n cycles in the chooser. The default is
.BR "all urls paths words lines" .
.TP
.B @extract_revamped_scope
The text to read:
.B pane
for the pane the key was pressed in,
.B all-panes
for every pane of its window, or
.B last-log
for the newest file in the log folder. The default is
.BR pane .
.TP
.B @extract_revamped_log_dir
The folder
.B last-log
reads. The default is
.IR ~/.tmux/logging-revamped .
.TP
.B @extract_revamped_custom_regex
The extended regex of the custom mode.
.TP
.B @extract_revamped_command
The shell command the run action starts, with each pick as "$1", "$2" and so
on, such as
.BR "git show \(dq$1\(dq" .
.TP
.B @extract_revamped_min_length
Drop tokens shorter than this. The default is
.BR 0 .
.TP
.B @extract_revamped_reverse
.B 1
puts the last match on screen first. The default is
.BR 0 .
.TP
.B @extract_revamped_multi
.B 1
lets fzf mark several tokens. The default is
.BR 0 .
.TP
.B @extract_revamped_osc52
.B 1
copies with an OSC 52 sequence instead of a clipboard tool. The default is
.BR 0 .
.TP
.B @extract_revamped_frecency
.B 1
puts recent picks first and keeps the last 20 in
.BR @extract_revamped_recent .
The default is
.BR 0 .
.TP
.B @extract_revamped_lines
Scrollback lines read above the screen. The default is
.BR 200 .
.TP
.BR @extract_revamped_popup_width ", " @extract_revamped_popup_height
The popup size. The defaults are
.B 80%
and
.BR 60% .
.TP
.B @revamped_theme
The theme of every tmux-revamped tool, when nothing else sets one. The default
is
.BR kodougu .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR fzf (1),
.BR gum (1)
